\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Two routes for one coefficient}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [connection difference](fdip-006D) compares two vertex
values after transporting one to the other. A cubical cochain also
has coefficients on edges and higher cells. Assigning each
coefficient to its labeled base corner puts the comparisons in
one module. On a square there are two transport paths between
opposite corners, as in the [plaquette holonomy](fdip-006N).
Which product rule respects these paths, and when does the square
of the resulting cochain differential vanish?}
